## 🗑️ Cleanup / Destroy Resources

### Destroy All Resources
```bash
# Destroy everything (CAUTION!)
terraform destroy

# Destroy specific resources
terraform destroy -target=module.sql_database
```

### Selective Cleanup
```bash
# Remove just the SQL database to save costs
terraform apply -var="create_sql_database=false"
```

## 🐛 Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

#### 1. "Subscription not registered"
```bash
az provider register --namespace Microsoft.Databricks
az provider register --namespace Microsoft.EventHub
az provider register --namespace Microsoft.Storage
```

#### 2. "Name already exists"
Storage account names must be globally unique. Edit `terraform.tfvars`:
```hcl
# The random suffix will help make it unique
# Or you can manually adjust the name pattern in modules/storage/main.tf
```

#### 3. "Insufficient permissions"
Ensure you have `Contributor` or `Owner` role:
```bash
az role assignment list --assignee $(az account show --query user.name -o tsv)
```

#### 4. "Key Vault access denied"
Your user needs access policy:
```bash
KEY_VAULT=$(terraform output -raw key_vault_name)
az keyvault set-policy \
  --name $KEY_VAULT \
  --upn $(az account show --query user.name -o tsv) \
  --secret-permissions get list set delete
```

### Debug Mode
```bash
# Enable Terraform debug logging
export TF_LOG=DEBUG
terraform plan

# Disable debug logging
unset TF_LOG
```

## 📝 Best Practices

### 1. State Management
```bash
# For team collaboration, use remote backend
# Uncomment the backend block in main.tf and create:
az storage account create --name sttfstatequickbuy --resource-group rg-terraform-state
az storage container create --name tfstate --account-name sttfstatequickbuy
```

### 2. Separate Environments
```bash
# Use workspaces for multiple environments
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace new prod

# Switch environments
terraform workspace select dev
```

### 3. Variable Management
```bash
# Use environment variables for sensitive data
export TF_VAR_sql_admin_password="YourPassword123!"
terraform apply
```

### 4. Version Control
Add to `.gitignore`:
```
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
```

